From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Open Video Tools contributors <noreply@ovt.dev>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avutil: add AV_FRAME_DATA_VIDEO_BLOCK_PARAMS side data

AV_FRAME_DATA_VIDEO_ENC_PARAMS exports only the final quantiser of each
block. Analysis tools also need the per-block syntax as signalled in the
bitstream: block partitioning, prediction modes and directions, reference
indices, coded block pattern, transform size, field decoding and motion
vector differences.

Add a new frame side data type carrying that syntax, modelled on
AVVideoEncParams: a self-describing header (AVVideoBlockParamsHeader)
followed by an array of fixed-size, type-specific block records reached
through blocks_offset/block_size with an inline accessor, so new fields can
be appended to a record without breaking the ABI. The first type is
AV_VIDEO_BLOCK_PARAMS_H264 with one AVH264MacroblockParams per macroblock.

A following patch exports it from the h264 decoder behind a new
export_side_data flag. This one adds the libavutil API, the side data name,
the minor version bump, the APIchanges entry and a FATE test
(fate-video_block_params) that round-trips 8160 macroblocks (1920x1088)
through frame side data.

Upstream-Status: Pending [to be submitted to ffmpeg-devel by OVT WI-4.103]
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Open Video Tools contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Rationale: FFmpeg's h264 decoder exports MVs and per-MB QP only; Open Video
  Tools needs mb_type, sub_mb_type, ref_idx, intra modes, cbp, mb_qp_delta
  and mvd (OVT spec chapter 07 section 7.6.3). Part 1 of 2 (OVT WI-4.100);
  part 2 (h264 decoder export) is OVT WI-4.101.
